  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Carpool Ledger",
    "overview": "Pool should read like a well-kept family ledger: every ride, driver, consent and handoff is written down plainly, and you can tell at a glance what's settled and what isn't. The palette is a soft sage paper world (Morning Paper canvas, Sage Mist sidebar, white panels on hairline borders) with one deep, trustworthy Ledger Green for primary actions and \"covered\" states. Harvest Amber is the only color that asks for attention, so an uncovered ride or a pending task stands out without raising alarm.\n\nComponents are friendly and tactile. Panels are generously rounded and padded, controls have a full 44px touch target, and lime icon discs and colored avatar initials add warmth without decoration. Density is moderate. It's an operational app read on a phone between errands, so each card carries one fact cluster, and the multi-column grid only appears once there's room for it.\n\nThe system is flat. Depth comes from tonal layering (paper → mist → white) and 1px hairlines, never shadows. The UI is set in two typefaces: Manrope for tight, confident headings and DM Sans for calm, readable body text.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
